{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. You’re here because of nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:15:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I woke up this morning vomiting. I’ve had cramps and four loose stools. I feel really anxious too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:16:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You have type 1 diabetes—did you take your insulin last night?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I took my Lantus. But not this morning. I couldn’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:18:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your blood sugar in the ER—it was high at 390. You also had ketones, and your anion gap was elevated. That means you were in mild DKA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. Is that why I feel so awful?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:20:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. We started IV fluids and insulin to correct it. Your gap is already improving. But we also need to find out why this happened."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could it be the stomach bug I’ve had before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:23:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We did a CT scan to rule out serious causes like bowel ischemia. Good news—it showed no blockages or dangerous issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:24:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But I’ve been having this cough too. Could that be related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:25:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT did show some small opacities in your right lung—likely bronchiolitis, which is a mild lung infection. It might be part of what triggered the DKA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:26:55",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So both my stomach and lungs are involved?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:28:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We think you have a viral infection affecting your gut—like viral gastritis. That, plus the lung issue, likely caused the DKA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:29:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need more tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2123-11-10 01:30:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring your labs. You’re on IV fluids and insulin now. Once you can eat, we’ll switch to your regular insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2123-11-10 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar is coming down, and your ketones are clearing. But your nausea is still bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2123-11-10 08:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still feel sick. I haven’t eaten anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2123-11-10 08:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you anti-nausea meds. We also noticed your hemoglobin is a bit low. We’ll check your stool for blood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2123-11-10 08:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been vomiting so much—could that be causing it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2123-11-10 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Repeated vomiting can irritate your stomach and cause minor bleeding. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2123-11-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood work shows your DKA has resolved. But you’re still not eating. We’re concerned about why this keeps happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2123-11-11 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just can’t keep food down. It’s been like this before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2123-11-11 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history, GI wants to do an endoscopy to look inside your stomach. It might help explain the vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2123-11-11 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe? I’m feeling weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2123-11-11 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s routine. You’ll be sedated. We’ll check for inflammation or other issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2123-11-14 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The endoscopy is done. We saw mild redness at the junction of your esophagus and stomach, and patchy redness in the stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2123-11-14 12:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2123-11-14 12:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not dangerous. It’s likely from repeated vomiting. We took biopsies to check for H. pylori or gastritis. Results are pending."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2123-11-14 12:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an ulcer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2123-11-14 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No ulcers seen. And no food was stuck in your stomach, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2123-11-14 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also got your chest X-ray. No pneumonia, but it supports the CT finding of bronchiolitis—likely viral."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2123-11-14 14:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been coughing. Should I be on antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2123-11-14 14:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because of your DKA and vomiting, we gave you a 5-day course of levofloxacin just in case. You’ve finished it now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2123-11-14 14:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been feeling anxious too—more than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2123-11-14 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had a few panic attacks this week. We started you on citalopram 10 mg daily. We’ve increased it to 20 mg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2123-11-14 14:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help? I don’t want to keep ending up here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2123-11-14 14:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should help over time. But you’ll need to follow up with your PCP to keep taking it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—you’ve been able to eat without vomiting. Your blood sugar is stable, and you’re off IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. Can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you today. We’re sending you home with a few changes to your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you from Protonix to pantoprazole—same type of medicine, but better for long-term use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve lowered your Lantus to 20 units at bedtime. Check your sugars before meals and at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if they’re still high?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If your fasting sugar is over 120 for three days in a row, increase your Lantus by 2 units every three days until it’s under 120."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about the citalopram?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking 20 mg daily. You must follow up with your PCP to continue it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my back pain? Oxycodone helped before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tried tramadol this time. It’s safer with your anxiety meds. If it helped, call your PCP. But avoid narcotics—they can worsen nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t know that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, narcotics can slow your stomach and make vomiting worse, especially with diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ll follow up with my doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Also, watch for fever, worsening pain, or vomiting. If they come back, call your PCP or come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We also made an outpatient GI appointment to discuss a gastric emptying study, since this keeps happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds helpful. I want to get to the bottom of this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And keep checking your sugars. You did well getting through this episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:26:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it’s over. I’ll take care of myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2123-11-15 07:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send all instructions with you. You’re cleared to go home when you’re ready."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2123-11-10 01:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2123-11-15 18:01:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes was admitted for nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, and diarrhea, found to be in mild diabetic ketoacidosis triggered by a viral gastroenteritis and bronchiolitis. She was treated with IV fluids and insulin, which resolved the DKA. An upper endoscopy showed mild esophagitis and gastric erythema likely from vomiting, with biopsies pending for H. pylori. She received a course of levofloxacin for bronchiolitis and was started on citalopram for anxiety and panic attacks. Her Lantus dose was reduced to 20 units at discharge to prevent hypoglycemia, and she was advised to follow up with her PCP for mental health and GI evaluation, including a possible gastric emptying study. She was discharged home in stable condition, tolerating oral intake, with instructions to monitor blood glucose and avoid narcotics.",
    "problems": [
      "Intestinal infection due to other organism, not elsewhere classified",
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Acute bronchiolitis due to other infectious organisms",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
